 # LOD Download Manager
-
 ## Overview
 The LOD Download Manager is a component of the Reall3D Viewer that manages the asynchronous, prioritized downloading of 3D Gaussian splat data organized in a Level of Detail (LOD) hierarchy [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently loading large-scale splat clouds over variable network connections by fetching metadata, resolving file URLs, and scheduling downloads based on camera proximity and device constraints [S1, unofficial]. It differs from static LOD selection by adapting to viewport position to prioritize splats that contribute most to the current user view, ensuring the highest visual fidelity for nearby tiles first [S1, unofficial].
